**Required changes to proto/monoterminal.proto:**

```protobuf
message AttachRequest {
  string session_id = 1;
  optional string auth_token = 2;  // ADD THIS
}

message InputData {
  string session_id = 1;
  bytes data = 2;
  optional string auth_token = 3;  // ADD THIS
}

message ResizeRequest {
  string session_id = 1;
  uint32 cols = 2;
  uint32 rows = 3;
  optional string auth_token = 4;  // ADD THIS
}
```

**After proto update:**
1. Regenerate Rust code: `protoc --rust_out=crates/protocol/src/generated proto/monoterminal.proto`
2. Verify no compilation errors in protocol crate
3. Report completion

**Timeline:** ~30 minutes (parallel track with build fixes)

**Dependencies:** security-engineer is waiting on this to wire JWT verification into handlers (critical path for criteria #2, #5)

**Coordination:** This change should not break existing code (fields are optional). Existing messages without tokens will have `None` values, which security-engineer will handle as "no auth provided" → error.

